    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-13932" textLabel="methionine adenosyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="P93438" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="1301.1456298828125" centerY="171.9304656982422" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi, O-27, pujar">A cDNA library prepared from rice seedling was screened using a carnation SAMS cDNA as a heterologous probe |CITS: [9375784]|. Two cDNAs were identified, isolated, and sequenced. One of those clones, SAMS1, has been reported previously |CITS: [7972513]|, while the other clone, named SAMS2, was novel. The deduced amino acid sequences are very similar (90-94%) to the homologous enzymes from other plants, and are 60-62% identical to enzymes from yeast, rat and human |CITS: [9375784]|. SAMS2 transcripts continuously accumulated during growth, up to the 14-day-growth period tested. Accumulation of the transcript was induced by NaCl treatment, suggesting the enzyme may play a role in the response of the cells to salt stress |CITS: [9375784]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-13932" />
